# Jewelry Hub - FYP Technical Rules & Context

## Project Overview
- A high-end Jewelry Management System for a family business (UK University Final Year Project).
- Roles: Admin (Web Dashboard), Artisan (Mobile), Customer (Mobile).

## Tech Stack
- Backend: Laravel (REST API & Admin Web Panel).
- Frontend: Flutter (Multi-role Mobile App).
- Real-time: Firebase (Chat & Order Progress Tracking).
- Database: MySQL.

## Business Logic & Unit Standards
- Base Currency: **MMK** — stored monetary amounts (catalog labor/gems, gold snapshots, quote/order lines, totals) are in Myanmar Kyat.
- FX Snapshot: `mmk_per_usd` (MMK per 1 USD) for deriving USD display and frozen `*_usd_snapshot` fields on quotes/orders.
- Display Currencies: MMK (primary in app) and USD (derived); optional GBP later via conversion.
- Weight Unit: Base unit is Grams.
- Local Display: Support Myanmar units (16.606g = 1 Kyat, 16 Pae = 1 Kyat, 8 Yway = 1 Pae).
- Pricing: Total MMK = (Weight × Live Gold MMK/gram) + Labor (MMK) + Gems (MMK).
- Catalog **list prices** require **active** gold + FX snapshots (`GET /api/v1/catalog/products` → `meta.pricing_configured`). After `php artisan db:seed`, **`PricingSnapshotSeeder`** (before **`CatalogSeeder`**) supplies demo snapshots so the mobile **`PriceTag`** is numeric, not “Price on request”.

## Development Rules
- Database First: Always define migrations before implementing features.
- Documentation: Every major implementation must be logged in `docs/FYP_Technical_Log.md`.
- Localization: Use a conversion service/provider for all currency and weight displays.
- Real-time: Use Firebase Streams for Chat and Progress Updates in Flutter.

## Global UI Standard (Flutter)
- **Theme**: Premium **Dark Gold** — primary `#D4AF37`, background `#0F172A`, elevated surfaces slate (`#1E293B` / `#334155`).
- **Glassmorphism**: Use shared glass cards — `BackdropFilter` blur, thin semi-transparent **gold** border, layered gradient fills (no flat gray slabs for primary surfaces).
- **Typography**: Distinctive pairing — display/brand via **Cinzel Decorative** (or equivalent), body/UI via **Outfit**; hierarchy: display > headline > body > caption (see `frontend/lib/core/ui/design_system.dart`).
- **Motion**: Prefer short fades (`AnimatedSwitcher` / `FadeTransition`) when switching **currency** or **weight units**; avoid jarring snaps.
- **Mandatory reuse**: New Flutter screens **must** use `frontend/lib/core/ui/design_system.dart` (`AppColors`, `AppTheme`, `AppGradients`, radii) and widgets under `frontend/lib/core/ui/widgets/` (`AppGlassCard`, `AppGoldButton`, `PremiumText`, `PriceTag`, `WeightBadge`) unless a one-off is explicitly justified in the task.
- **Auth (Flutter)**: Sanctum **bearer token** in **`flutter_secure_storage`** (`AuthTokenStorage`); session state in **`AuthProvider`** (`frontend/lib/core/providers/auth_provider.dart`). API calls live under **`frontend/lib/features/auth/data/auth_api.dart`**. The app **gates** the home stack: signed-out users see **login/register**; after sign-in, **customer catalog** is the default shell (admin/artisan can still sign in for testing; role-specific mobile homes can branch later). Use **`AuthProvider.token`** for new authenticated `http` clients.
- **Inquiries & chat (luxury standard)**: Treat inquiry chat as a **concierge** surface, not a spreadsheet or generic admin table. Reuse **`AppGlassCard`**, **`PremiumText`**, **`AppTheme.darkGold()`**, and inquiry widgets under **`features/inquiries/`**; **customer** message bubbles lean **gold** (`#D4AF37` family); **shop/concierge** bubbles lean **glass / slate** with gold borders — see **`frontend/lib/core/ui/design_system.dart`**.
- **Inquiries & chat (technical)**: Customer **`features/inquiries/`** + **`CustomerShell`** (catalog + inquiries tabs). Firestore path **`inquiry_threads/{firebase_thread_id}/messages`** (and optionally **`typing`**, thread-level metadata for **pipeline status**). Laravel **`POST /api/v1/conversations/{inquiry}/firebase-bootstrap`**, **`firebase-token`**, and related APIs mint/sync as documented in **`docs/FYP_Technical_Log.md`**. Filament **`InquiryResource`** + **`ChatInquiry`** / slide-over chat for admin — **same Firebase thread** as Flutter. Configure Firebase per **`docs/Firebase_Setup.md`** and deploy **`firebase/firestore.rules`** whenever message shape or subcollections change.
- **Quotes & orders (bespoke)**: **`POST /api/v1/quotes/{id}/accept`** uses **`OrderBuilderService::acceptSentQuoteAndCreateOrder`**. If the quote has **`inquiry_id`**, all other **non-cancelled** orders on that inquiry are **superseded**: **confirmed** deposit **`Payment`** rows are **reparented** to the new order (never deleted); all deposit-type payments move with the order id; prior orders are **`cancelled`**. Other **`accepted`** quotes on the inquiry are **voided**. **`deposit_amount_mmk`** on the new order = **`max(0, required_deposit − sum(confirmed deposit amounts))`** where required = **`default_deposit_percentage`** × quote **`total_mmk`**; if **zero** due, status **`deposit_confirmed`**. If credited ≥ order **`total_mmk`**, treat deposit milestone as satisfied (**`deposit_confirmed`**). **Admin** **`POST /api/v1/admin/orders`** uses **`createFromQuote`** with the same supersede rules. **Payment card `amount_mmk`** = additional deposit still due; optional breakdown keys **`order_total_mmk`**, **`credited_deposit_mmk`**, **`balance_remaining_mmk`**, **`additional_deposit_due_mmk`** from **`InquiryPipelinePresenter::paymentBalanceBreakdown`**.
- **Quote publish advisor (`InquiryQuoteCommitmentGate`)**: Publishing is **never 422**. When a **confirmed** deposit exists on an active order for the inquiry, responses may include **`meta.warning`** (REST) or Filament **warning** notification: *"A deposit is already confirmed. A new quote will recalculate the balance."*
- **Artisan alerts**: **`notifications`** table (Laravel); **`QuoteRevisedAcceptedForArtisan`** when a superseding accept migrates assignments. **`GET /api/v1/artisan/notifications`** for polling. Active **`order_assignments`** (**`assigned`/`in_progress`**) are moved to the **new** **`order_id`** with **`order_item_id`** cleared and instructions appended (*Quote revised — review design changes.*).
- **Production & QC lifecycle**: Filament **Order detail** includes **Assign artisan** and **QC approve** actions (resource under **`app/Filament/Resources/Orders/`**). Reuse **`OrderLifecycleService`** for assignment/start/review/QC guards so API + Filament enforce the same transitions. Starting production requires **`deposit_confirmed`** + a confirmed deposit payment. QC approve transitions **`pending_qc -> ready`** only.
- **QC chat message**: On QC approve, backend posts a Firestore text message to the inquiry thread: **`Your order has passed Quality Control and is now Ready for Collection!`** (non-blocking if Firestore client is unavailable).
- **Artisan mobile notifications**: Flutter artisan app includes `ArtisanNotificationsScreen`; tapping a notification resolves by `order_id` and deep-links to `ArtisanJobDetailScreen` when a matching assignment exists.
- **Pipeline API**: **`GET /api/v1/inquiries/{inquiry}`** → **`meta.pipeline`** includes **`deposit_payment`** (MySQL mirror of payment-instruction fields) when the latest order is **`awaiting_deposit`** and a deposit profile exists—Flutter may show **`InquiryPaymentInfoCard`** from REST when Firestore has no `payment_info_card`. Refresh pipeline when Firestore thread/messages update if fallbacks must stay in sync.
- **Filament chat**: **`chat-inquiry.blade.php`** renders **server-side quote/payment cards** from **`$adminQuoteCardPayload`** + **`$pipeline['deposit_payment']`** into **`#jh-server-cards`**; JS skips duplicate Firestore messages for the same **`quote_id`** / **`order_number`**. After quote publish / payment send, **`jhAdminChatRefreshStatic`** runs on delayed **`setTimeout`** so Livewire-morphed JSON is read correctly.
- **Source of truth**: **MySQL** holds **`inquiries`**, **`quotes`**, **`orders`**, **`payments`**, and formal statuses; **Firebase** is for **real-time chat** and (when the PHP Firestore client is available) **server-written** `quote_card` / `payment_info_card` / thread metadata. Prefer **one business rule in Laravel**; Firestore is delivery, not the ledger. Do not duplicate business rules only in Firestore.
- **Backend admin (web)**: Filament panel at `/admin`; primary color aligned to `#D4AF37` for consistency with the app. **Pricing** sidebar: **Gold prices** + **Exchange rates** (create new snapshots via `PricingService`; history is read-only in the UI).

## Architecture
- Root Directory:
  /backend (Laravel)
  /frontend (Flutter)
  /docs (Documentation)